    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0274" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg224"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Vignaud to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received July 23.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 190.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Eustis’s No. 184, of July
                    3, reporting that your telegram relative to the religious service to be held in
                    Washington in memory of the late President Carnot had been communicated to the
                    minister for foreign affairs, I have now to state that this communication was
                    acknowledged by Mr. Hanotaux under date of the 7th instant. The Government of
                    the Republic, he says, was very much touched by the part taken at Washington
                    with France in her mourning, and he asks that its thanks be conveyed to our
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Vignaud.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
